✅️ 26. Alternate Even-Odd Printing — Thread Approach

🎗️ 26.1 Problem Statement

Print numbers from 1 to N using two threads:

👉 Even-Thread → prints even numbers.
👉 Odd-Thread → prints odd numbers.
👉 Output must be in sequential order.

👉 Expected Output

For N = 10:

Odd-Thread:1
Even-Thread:2
Odd-Thread:3
Even-Thread:4
Odd-Thread:5
Even-Thread:6
Odd-Thread:7
Even-Thread:8
Odd-Thread:9
Even-Thread:10

With the provided code, execution starts with number = 1, so Odd-Thread prints 1 first.
The scheduler determines which thread enters first, but the synchronization conditions ensure the numbers are printed in the correct order.

