👉 SharedResource.java

public class SharedResource {

    private int number;
    private final int limit;

    public SharedResource(int number, int limit) {
        this.number = number;
        this.limit = limit;
    }

    public synchronized void printEven() {
        while (number <= limit) {
            while (number % 2 != 0) {
                try {
                    wait();
                } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                    Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                    return;
                }
            }

            if (number > limit) {
                break;
            }

            System.out.println(Thread.currentThread().getName()+ ":" + number);
            number++;
            notify();
    }

    public synchronized void printOdd() {
        while (number <= limit) {
            while (number % 2 == 0) {
                try {
                    wait();
                } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                    Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                    return;
                }
            }

            if (number > limit) {
                break;
            }

            System.out.println(Thread.currentThread().getName() + ":" + number);
            number++;
            notify();
        }
    }
}



🎗️ 26.13 Dry Run

👉 Assume:

🔴 number = 1
🔴 limit = 4

👉 Step 1
🔴 number = 1
🔴 Odd Thread gets the monitor.

1 % 2 == 0 → false
🔴 So it prints: Odd-Thread:1

Then:

number++;
notify();

Now:
number = 2

👉 Step 2

🔴 Odd Thread checks again. 2 % 2 == 0 → true

So:
wait();

🔴 Odd Thread releases the monitor.
🔴 Even Thread acquires it.

👉 Step 3

🔴 Even Thread checks: 2 % 2 != 0 → false

So it prints:
Even-Thread:2

Then:

number++;
notify();

Now:
number = 3

👉 Step 4

🔴 Even Thread checks again. 3 % 2 != 0 → true
🔴 So Even Thread waits.
🔴 Odd Thread wakes up and prints: Odd-Thread:3

Then:
number = 4
notify();

👉 Step 5

🔴 Even Thread wakes and prints: Even-Thread:4

Then:
number = 5

Since:
5 > 4

🔴 both threads eventually exit.

