🎗️ 26.15 Why Does the Solution Work?

🔴 The solution works because both threads use the same SharedResource object.
🔴 The shared number is protected by synchronized methods.

One Shared Object
       ↓
One Monitor
       ↓
One Shared Counter
       ↓
Two Coordinated Threads

🔴 Each thread waits when it is not its turn and wakes the other thread after updating the shared state.

🎗️ 26.16 Role of Each Component

-------------------------------------------------------
| Component        | Responsibility                   |
| ---------------- | -------------------------------- |
| `SharedResource` | Maintains shared state           |
| `number`         | Current number                   |
| `limit`          | Maximum number                   |
| `printEven()`    | Prints even numbers              |
| `printOdd()`     | Prints odd numbers               |
| `EvenThread`     | Executes `printEven()`           |
| `OddThread`      | Executes `printOdd()`            |
| `synchronized`   | Provides mutual exclusion        |
| `wait()`         | Waits for its turn               |
| `notify()`       | Wakes the other thread           |
| `join()`         | Makes main wait for both threads |
