🎗️ 26.17 Why join()?

In the main method:

thread1.join();
thread2.join();

join() makes the main thread wait until both worker threads finish.

Main Thread
     ↓
start Even
     ↓
start Odd
     ↓
join()
     ↓
Wait for both threads
     ↓
Both complete
     ↓
Main continues

🎗️ 26.19 Common Mistakes

❌ Creating separate SharedResource objects
❌ Using different locks for even and odd threads
❌ Using if instead of while with wait()
❌ Forgetting notify()
❌ Calling run() instead of start()
❌ Modifying number outside synchronization
❌ Forgetting the termination condition
❌ Busy waiting instead of wait()

🎗️ 26.20 Complexity

For printing N numbers:

Time Complexity  : O(N)
Space Complexity : O(1)

Two threads are used, but the total number of printing operations is still proportional to N.
